  "### Why Violations Exist",
  "",
  "1. **Data source discrepancies:** ffanalytics may scrape player projections before",
  "   the player exists in the NFL API",
  "2. **Manual data entry:** Some player IDs are added manually (see `missing_player_ids.rds`)",
  "3. **Legacy data:** Historical data may have incomplete ID mapping",
  "",
  "---",
  "",
  "## ffa_db.rds Violations",
  "",
  "### ffa_players → ffa_player_ids",
  "",
  "**Issue:** Some players in `ffa_players` don't have entries in `ffa_player_ids`.",
  "",
  "**Impact:** Cannot map these players to external systems (NFL API, ESPN, CBS, etc.)",
  "",
  "**Mitigation:**",
  "1. Use `missing_player_ids.rds` as supplement",
  "2. Use `left_join()` instead of `inner_join()`",
  "3. Accept NA values for external IDs",
  "",
  "**Example:**",
  "```r",
  "# Load supplement",
  "missing_ids <- readRDS('app/2023_compliance/missing_player_ids.rds')",
  "",
  "# Consolidate",
  "all_ids <- bind_rows(",
  "  ffa_db$ffa_player_ids,",
  "  missing_ids",
  ")",
  "",
  "# Safe join",
  "ffa_db$ffa_players %>%",
  "  left_join(all_ids, by = 'id')  # Preserves unmatched players",
  "```",
  "",
  "### ffa_projtable → ffa_players",
  "",
  "**Issue:** Some projections reference (id, pos) combinations not in `ffa_players`.",
  "",
  "**Impact:** Cannot get full player metadata for these projections.",
  "",
  "**Mitigation:** Use left joins and accept partial metadata",
  "",
  "```r",
  "ffa_db$ffa_projtable %>%",
  "  left_join(ffa_db$ffa_players, by = c('id', 'pos')) %>%",
  "  # first_name, last_name may be NA for some rows",
  "  filter(!is.na(first_name))  # Or keep NAs and handle downstream",
  "```",
  "",
  "---",
  "",
  "## Finding Violation Details",
  "",
  "### Identify missing player IDs",
  "",
  "```r",
  "# Players without ID mapping",
  "unmapped_players <- ffa_db$ffa_players %>%",
  "  anti_join(ffa_db$ffa_player_ids, by = 'id') %>%",
  "  select(id, first_name, last_name, team, position) %>%",
  "  arrange(last_name, first_name)",
  "",
  "# Count by position",
  "unmapped_players %>%",
  "  count(position, sort = TRUE)",
  "```",
  "",
  "### Check projection coverage",
  "",
  "```r",
  "# Projections without player metadata",
  "orphan_projections <- ffa_db$ffa_projtable %>%",
  "  anti_join(ffa_db$ffa_players, by = c('id', 'pos')) %>%",
  "  distinct(id, pos) %>%",
  "  arrange(pos, id)",
  "```",
  "",
  "---",
  "",
  "## Best Practices",
  "",
  "1. **Always use left joins** when connecting ffa tables",
  "2. **Check for NAs** after joins and decide handling strategy",
  "3. **Use missing_player_ids.rds** as supplemental data source",
  "4. **Document assumptions** when dropping NA rows",
  "",
  "### Good Example",
  "",
  "```r",
  "# Defensive join with clear NA handling",
  "analysis_data <- ffa_db$ffa_projtable %>%",
  "  filter(season == 2025, week == 17) %>%",
  "  left_join(ffa_db$ffa_players, by = c('id', 'pos')) %>%",
  "  mutate(",
  "    player_label = case_when(",
  "      !is.na(first_name) ~ glue('{first_name} {last_name}'),",
  "      TRUE ~ glue('Unknown Player {id}')",
  "    )",
  "  )",
  "```",
  "",
  "### Bad Example",
  "",
  "```r",
  "# ❌ Silent data loss",
  "analysis_data <- ffa_db$ffa_projtable %>%",
  "  inner_join(ffa_db$ffa_players, by = c('id', 'pos'))  # Drops unmapped players",
  "```",
  "",
  "---",
  "",
  paste("**Document Version:**", Sys.time())
)

writeLines(fk_violations, file.path(OUTPUT_DIR, "FK_VIOLATIONS.md"))
